 "post": {
  "title": "What IP68 really protects",
  "caption": "What IP68 on your phone really means 💧\n\nThe 6: dust tight, no dust gets in.\nThe 8: fresh water, at a depth and time the maker tests. New iPhones (iPhone 16 and later) are rated to 6 m for up to 30 minutes, tested in a lab.\nNot for: swimming, showers, saunas, salt water.\nThe seals wear with normal use, so the rating is not permanent.\n\nIP68 saves a spill, not a swim. Send this to the friend who takes their phone in the pool.",
  "keywords": [
   "what does IP68 mean",
   "IP68 water resistance",
   "is my phone waterproof",
   "IP68 phone underwater",
   "phone water damage",
   "IP rating explained"
  ],
  "hashtags": [
   "#ip68",
